              "description": "The September-October 02005 issue of The Taxpayer Magazine. Highlights include: Saskatchewan News  discovers that First Nations University of Canada (which yours truly lived across the road from from 02012 to 02015) has a board of directors that pays itself nearly 9X more than the board of directors of the University of Regina does, despite having a fraction the number of students and available courses Environment Canada persecutes Leduc greenskeeper Peter Francis for moving geese off of the Alberta golf course at which he works, with a potential punishment of a fine of $300K & a six-month prison sentence Canada's mortgage monopoly by the CMHC the history of state control over liquor sales in Canada, and Alberta's results in privatising it the freebies that Citizenship and Immigration Canada gives to refugees, and which ten countries furnished Canada with the most refugees in 02003 potential good news for Winnipeg with their new mayor Sam Katz and much more!",
